        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs a comparator for the given operands. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The result is computed from the arguments, before they are forwarded to the base. The tag argument is used only to deduce <computeroutput>Compare_T</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>L</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the left-hand operand argument. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>R</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the right-hand operand argument.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The left-hand operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The right-hand operand.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Evaluates the comparison inside an immediately invoked lambda, which converts the result of <computeroutput>Compare_T::apply()</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, and passes it to the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op" kindref="compound">binary_op</ref></computeroutput> base class constructor:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>for the framework constants with static <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref></computeroutput> members (the numeric literals), the two values are compared directly;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>if at least one operand is a framework floating-point wrapper with an <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput> member, and the tag defines a <computeroutput>within_tolerance_result</computeroutput> (all the built-in tags do), operands within the tolerance give this result; otherwise the unwrapped values are compared; the tags of the application without it ignore the tolerance;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>for all other types, the framework wrappers are unwrapped, and the values, including the types of the application, are compared as they are. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
