    <briefdescription>
<para>Relational comparator struct template. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op" kindref="compound">binary_op</ref></computeroutput>, this struct compares the left-hand operand with the right-hand operand, using the operator defined by the tag <computeroutput>Compare_T</computeroutput> (<computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1equal__to" kindref="compound">equal_to</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1not__equal__to" kindref="compound">not_equal_to</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1greater" kindref="compound">greater</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1greater__equal" kindref="compound">greater_equal</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1less" kindref="compound">less</ref></computeroutput>, or <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1less__equal" kindref="compound">less_equal</ref></computeroutput>). It is used within test expressions to provide human-readable relational checks, with the actual and expected values, and the symbol of the tag, reported upon failure.</para>
<para>The tag is passed as an empty constructor argument, so that all three template arguments are deduced, for example <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1compare__op" kindref="compound">compare_op</ref>{ <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1a27b015b0e2b40e0f0bbb1b08588e1c20" kindref="member">lhs</ref>, <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1ae1436f1b38c1062f7c733d3e8cb39b87" kindref="member">rhs</ref>, <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1equal__to" kindref="compound">equal_to</ref>{} }</computeroutput>. A factory function would do the same, but at <computeroutput>-O0</computeroutput> it adds one function per instantiation.</para>
<para>It is also public, as <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1compare__op" kindref="compound">extension::compare_op</ref></computeroutput>, so that the applications can define their own comparisons with their own tags. A tag is an empty struct with:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>a <computeroutput>static constexpr const char* symbol</computeroutput>, written between the operands in the failure reports, with the surrounding spaces (for example <computeroutput>" divides "</computeroutput>);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>a static <computeroutput>apply (<ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1a27b015b0e2b40e0f0bbb1b08588e1c20" kindref="member">lhs</ref>, <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1ae1436f1b38c1062f7c733d3e8cb39b87" kindref="member">rhs</ref>)</computeroutput> member function template, which receives the unwrapped operands (the values of the <computeroutput>to_*</computeroutput> wrappers and of the literals) and returns the result as <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>optionally, a <computeroutput>static constexpr bool within_tolerance_result</computeroutput>; when present, and an operand is a floating-point wrapper (see <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1has__epsilon" kindref="compound">extension::has_epsilon</ref></computeroutput>), the operands within the tolerance give this result, as for the built-in comparators; when absent, the tolerance is ignored.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The operands are reported as the built-in comparators report them: the stored operands are prepared by <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>, so the C strings are written quoted, and the arrays as ranges; the tag still receives the operands as they were passed, without this conversion.</para>
<para>The temporaries are moved into the comparator, and the named operands are copied (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ae9fe49cb0d38724533e9a27a2232bf09" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref></computeroutput>), so a comparator built in a function from its <computeroutput>const&amp;</computeroutput> parameters can be returned from it.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored left-hand operand, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored right-hand operand, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Compare_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The tag that defines the comparison. It is stateless, with a static <computeroutput>symbol</computeroutput> and a static <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput>, so a parameter, such as a tolerance, is passed as an operand, usually the right one, and reported with the operands. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
